\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces The simulation of a Michelson interferometer with thin a beamsplitter is shown in blue. The same simulation was done with a thick beam splitter, this is shown in orange. The analytic behaviour of a Michelson interferometer(equation \ref  {eq:michelson}) is shown by dashed black line. The tuning of one of the arm mirrors was changed and the power at the AS port was measured. Comparing the outputs of the simulation to equation \ref  {eq:michelson} shows that thick beamsplitters should be used.\relax }}{62}{figure.caption.85}}
\newlabel{fig:thinvsthick}{{3.1}{62}{The simulation of a Michelson interferometer with thin a beamsplitter is shown in blue. The same simulation was done with a thick beam splitter, this is shown in orange. The analytic behaviour of a Michelson interferometer(equation \ref {eq:michelson}) is shown by dashed black line. The tuning of one of the arm mirrors was changed and the power at the AS port was measured. Comparing the outputs of the simulation to equation \ref {eq:michelson} shows that thick beamsplitters should be used.\relax }{figure.caption.85}{}}
